  book_title: The Beauty of Southwest
  book_color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  book_clue_index: 114
  content: "This book offers a comprehensive overview of southwest\u2019s culture
    and scenery."
  clue_content: "A distinctive plant Anthophasma vespertinum grows in the region.
    Its petals resemble insect limbs and change shape in response to temperature
    and sunlight. Dried specimens are used in traditional medicine and are a local
    specialty.\nMany villages depend on cultivating this flower for their livelihood.
    Rising prices in recent years have attracted newcomers hoping to establish themselves
    in the local \u201Cinsect medicine\u201D trade."
